WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:07.210
Duane Lee Chapman, better known as "Dog the
Bounty Hunter," made a name for himself by

00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:10.330
bringing criminals to justice while urging
them to change their ways.

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:15.420
The tanned and mullet-topped reality television
star nabbed fugitives and scored major ratings

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:19.090
for over a decade before pretty much disappearing
from the airwaves.

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:21.360
But Dog hasn't been locked in a kennel.

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:24.710
This legend of liberty has remained active
across the American frontier.

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:27.910
Here's what he's been up to for the last few
years...

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:29.949
Uncaged Cage

00:00:29.949 --> 00:00:34.840
According to ABC News, New Orleans police
arrested actor Nicolas Cage in 2011, after

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:38.399
a domestic dispute with his wife Alice Kim
got a little out of hand.

00:00:38.399 --> 00:00:41.539
Dog, a fan of Cage's, later bailed him out
of jail.

00:00:41.539 --> 00:00:44.649
Charges against Cage were dropped later that
year, and we're still waiting for someone

00:00:44.649 --> 00:00:47.899
to make a TV series out of this burgeoning
friendship.

00:00:47.899 --> 00:00:48.899
Arrest warrant for Beth

00:00:48.899 --> 00:00:55.190
In 2013, Dog and his wife Beth Chapman's vacation
in Colorado was interrupted by a loud car.

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:58.929
According to TMZ, Beth shouted insults at
one of the passengers, before calling the

00:00:58.929 --> 00:01:01.730
police and leaving before officers arrived.

00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:05.659
The teenagers suffered no consequences...but
calling a person names is actually a crime

00:01:05.659 --> 00:01:07.070
in Colorado.

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:09.710
One passenger filed a harassment complaint
against Beth.

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:13.090
When she didn't pick up the summons, police
issued a warrant for her arrest.

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:16.719
She later turned herself in, saving Dog from
the awkward task of bringing his own wife

00:01:16.719 --> 00:01:18.310
to justice.

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:19.600
Dog talked about his time in prison

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:24.950
In 2015, Dog revealed that in 1976, he was
charged and convicted of the murder of an

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:26.590
alleged pimp and drug dealer.

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:29.969
Though Dog's friend pulled the trigger while
he was waiting in the car, Chapman received

00:01:29.969 --> 00:01:34.180
a five-year prison sentence, ultimately serving
18 months.

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:37.270
Years later, Chapman dealt with the incident
during an episode of Dog and Beth: On the

00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:42.380
Hunt's third season to show people it's possible
to turn your life around.

00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:44.740
Step-daughter arrested for bank robbery

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:49.950
According to Hawaii News Now, Dog's step-daughter
Nicole Gillespie allegedly robbed the downtown

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:53.289
Honolulu Territorial Savings Bank, in 2015.

00:01:53.289 --> 00:01:56.740
Upon learning of her arrest, Dog issued a
statement, revealing that Nicole had been

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:59.079
estranged from the rest of the family for
some time:

00:01:59.079 --> 00:02:03.189
"It's always difficult and disheartening when
someone you knew as a child grows up and chooses

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:06.520
a life of crime [...] We have not seen "Nickie"
in over 10 years.

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:09.479
Watching her on Crimestoppers left us all
shocked and heart broken."

00:02:09.479 --> 00:02:12.690
Ended his show to save bounty hunting

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:17.819
Chapman ended his three-season follow-up show
for CMT, Dog and Beth: On the Hunt, in 2015,

00:02:17.819 --> 00:02:21.260
saying he wanted to combat bail reform efforts
across America.

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:25.580
Calls for reform started after a rash of unfortunate
incidents, like a man being shot to death

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:27.550
by bounty hunters in Idaho.

00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:31.060
According to In Touch, Dog felt his energy
was better spent working to stop proposed

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:34.730
laws that included establishing requirements
such as minimum-age limits for bounty hunters

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:37.010
and licenses to carry concealed weapons.

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:39.510
And things are going Dog's way.

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:43.560
In 2016, according to the Idaho Press-Tribune,
his efforts helped defeat such a bill in Idaho,

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:46.760
almost one year after the death of the aforementioned
man.

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:49.129
He opposes Stand-Your-Ground laws

00:02:49.129 --> 00:02:52.900
During an interview with HuffPost Live, Dog
voiced his opinions on the sensitive topic

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:53.900
of gun control.

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:57.430
First, he sought to debunk the gun lobby's
argument that "the only thing that can stop

00:02:57.430 --> 00:03:00.090
a bad guy with a gun is a good guy with a
gun."

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:03.600
He insisted he's never used a gun on any of
the criminals he's caught—just tasers and

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:04.800
pepper spray.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:08.329
He also argued that so-called "stand your
ground" laws are "bullcrap."

00:03:08.329 --> 00:03:11.600
Not the opinions you'd expect to hear out
of a guy who looks like Chapman, or one in

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:12.600
his line of work.

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:17.349
Just goes to show you can't judge a book by
its cover...or a bounty hunter by his mullet.

00:03:17.349 --> 00:03:18.610
Cultural impact

00:03:18.610 --> 00:03:21.900
If you've watched this video to this point,
it's because you know all about our friend

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:25.000
Dog, and recognize him as more than just a
bounty hunter with beautiful hair.

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:28.189
That's because in the years since he first
took to television, he's become more than

00:03:28.189 --> 00:03:31.830
just a strong man bringing people to justice...he's
become a cultural icon.

00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:36.329
A real-life Boba Fett, he's been referenced
in shows like American Dad!, Family Guy, and

00:03:36.329 --> 00:03:37.329
South Park.

00:03:37.329 --> 00:03:40.810
And when a show as huge as The Simpsons makes
reference to you, you know your legacy is

00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:41.840
secure.

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:42.840
Thanks for watching!

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:45.629
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to see more
videos like the one you just saw.

00:03:45.629 --> 00:03:48.480
And leave us a comment to let us know if you
want to see Dog back on TV...

